---
number: 309
title: Lord, I Want to Be Made Holy
author: Anonymous
composer: J. Granahan
sp_category: "21"
topic: Hope and Aspiration
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Lord, I want to be made holy,
Give me now Thy purity;
In the blood of Jesus cleanse me,
That, like snow, I pure may be.

[chorus]
Make me holy, Lord, just now;
Cleanse my heart as here I bow.
Jesus, Lord, take my heart,
Never let me ever part.

[verse 2]
This my soul’s sincerest yearning;
Cleanse me from my guilt I pray;
Grant my heart’s desire by turning
Sinful night to sinless day.

[chorus]
Make me holy, Lord, just now;
Cleanse my heart as here I bow.
Jesus, Lord, take my heart,
Never let me ever part.

[verse 3]
In myself I have no goodness;
Without Thee, my strength is weak;
For Thy holiness I’m pleading,
Grace, through Jesus’ blood I seek.

[chorus]
Make me holy, Lord, just now;
Cleanse my heart as here I bow.
Jesus, Lord, take my heart,
Never let me ever part.

[verse 4]
Holy Father, to Thy presence
Penitent I come today;
Grant me, Lord, Thy boundless mercy,
Take my many sins away.

[chorus]
Make me holy, Lord, just now;
Cleanse my heart as here I bow.
Jesus, Lord, take my heart,
Never let me ever part.
